        "original_id": "18064269-4157-5375-bb38-e844538af389",
        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- People: J. Robert Oppenheimer\n- Organizations: United States Atomic Energy Commission, Los Alamos Laboratory\n- Projects: Manhattan Project\n- Events: Oppenheimer security hearing, World War II, atomic bombings of Hiroshima and Nagasaki\n- Concepts: atomic bomb, nuclear weapons\n\nFacts:\n- During World War II, J. Robert Oppenheimer headed the Los Alamos Laboratory.\n- During World War II, J. Robert Oppenheimer played a key role in the Manhattan Project.\n- The Manhattan Project developed the first nuclear weapons, including the atomic bombs used in the atomic bombings of Hiroshima and Nagasaki.\n- J. Robert Oppenheimer is among those credited as the \"father of the atomic bomb\" for his role in the Manhattan Project.\n- In 1954, the United States Atomic Energy Commission conducted the Oppenheimer security hearing.\n- The 1954 Oppenheimer security hearing examined the background, actions, and associations of J. Robert Oppenheimer.",
